                </td>
                <td width=572 valign=center colspan=10 style="width:343.6000pt;padding:0.0000pt 5.4000pt 0.0000pt 5.4000pt ;border-left:none;
mso-border-left-alt:none;border-right:1.0000pt solid windowtext;mso-border-right-alt:0.5000pt solid windowtext;
border-top:none;mso-border-top-alt:0.5000pt solid windowtext;border-bottom:1.0000pt solid windowtext;
mso-border-bottom-alt:0.5000pt solid windowtext;">
                    <p class=MsoNormal><span style="font-family:仿宋;mso-bidi-font-family:'Times New Roman';font-size:12.0000pt;
mso-font-kerning:1.0000pt;"><font face="仿宋"><p><span style="font-family: 'times new roman', times, serif;">“Medicinal Chemistry of Natural Products I” is a specialized course designed for undergraduate students majoring in pharmacy. Natural products are chemical substances derived from plants, animals, microorganisms, minerals, and other sources that can treat diseases and save lives. Natural product chemistry is a discipline that comprehensively applies modern scientific theories and methods to study the chemical constituents of natural products. The course covers the characterization of chemical constituents in natural products, their physicochemical properties, extraction and separation methods, structural identification techniques, and the confirmation of biological activity, with the aim of elucidating the molecular basis of pharmacological effects. </span></p>
<p><span style="font-family: 'times new roman', times, serif;">This course aims to equip students with a systematic understanding of the core theoretical knowledge and practical skills in the field of natural product chemistry, enabling them to develop the professional competence required for research and development, production, and related scientific work involving natural products, thereby laying the foundation for their future careers in the pharmaceutical industry or research institutions.</span></p>
<p>&nbsp;</p></font></span><span style="font-family:'Times New Roman';mso-fareast-font-family:仿宋;font-size:10.5000pt;
mso-font-kerning:1.0000pt;"><o:p></o:p></span></p>
                </td>
            </tr>
            <tr style="height:19.9000pt;">
                <td width=777 valign=center colspan=14 style="width:466.7000pt;padding:0.0000pt 5.4000pt 0.0000pt 5.4000pt ;border-left:1.0000pt solid windowtext;
